164: class SpectralMatrix(object):
165:     """
166:     Represents a spectral compensation matrix using the ordinary least squares
167:     method (OLS). Unlike conventional flow cytometry where one detector is
168:     used per fluorochrome, spectral flow cytometry utilizes a larger number of
169:     detectors than fluorochromes. The corresponding spectral matrix (M x N) is
170:     not square, with more columns than rows (N > M). The rows (M) in the matrix
171:     correspond to the "true" fluorochromes (i.e. those detectors with dedicated
172:     fluorochromes). Note, there is no inverse method for this method of
173:     compensation.
174: 
175:     :param spill_data_array: NumPy array of matrix data
